    "name": "Tenanting",
    "definition": "A deployment pattern in which each tenant's (customer's) data lives in its own database. ArgentSea models the tenant databases as the shards of a shard set, so tenant routing uses the same shard id, shard key and fan-out machinery as data sharding.",
    "synonyms": [
      "tenant isolation",
      "tenant database"
    ]
